hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"88","Yā Ḥayyu Yā Qayyūm, biraḥmatika astaghīth, aṣliḥ lī shaʾnī kullah, wa lā takilnī ilā nafsī ṭarfat ʿayn.. O Ever-Living, O Self-Sustaining, I seek help through Your mercy. Set right all my affairs, and do not leave me to myself even for the blink of an eye."
"89","Asbahna wa asbahal-mulku lillahi Rabbil-'alamin. Allahumma inni as'aluka khayra hadhal-yawm, fathahu, wa nasrahu, wa nurahu wa barakatahu, wa hudahu, wa a'udhu bika min sharri ma fihi wa sharri ma ba'dah. Wa idha amsa qala: Amsayna wa amsal-mulku lillahi Rabbil-'alamin. Allahumma inni as'aluka khayra hadhihil-laylah, fathaha, wa nasraha, wa nuraha wa barakataha, wa hudaha, wa a'udhu bika min sharri ma fiha wa sharri ma ba'daha.. We have reached the morning and the dominion belongs to Allah, the Lord of the worlds. O Allah, I ask You for the goodness of this day—its victory, its help, its light, its blessings, and its guidance—and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what is in it and the evil of what comes after it. And when evening comes, he says: We have reached the evening and the dominion belongs to Allah, the Lord of the worlds. O Allah, I ask You for the goodness of this night—its victory, its help, its light, its blessings, and its guidance—and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what is in it and the evil of what comes after it."
